**Read:** [Geological Structures: a Practical Introduction — Waldron and Snyder](../sources/Geological-Structures-Waldron-Snyder.lingua#r_2RC4KMK6ADFX90708NZH2F6RRW), Folds, Primary Structures, Fabrics, and Labs 4–5 in full; [Physical Geology, second edition — Steven Earle](../sources/Physical-Geology-Earle.lingua#r_5GWEYVQGR176TXMQT0S881ZSKX), chapter 12’s folding discussion; [Introduction to Historical Geology — Estrada and contributing authors](../sources/Introduction-to-Historical-Geology.lingua#r_1JKSSECEDW0M9QG30TJ1D9KHZD), structural relationships in regional histories.

Describe a fold's limbs, hinge line, axial surface, wavelength, amplitude, and geometry before proposing a mechanism. Antiform and synform describe shape; anticline and syncline require the stratigraphic age relations. Overturned or refolded successions make those distinctions consequential rather than merely terminological.

Younging or facing indicators constrain which way the original succession becomes younger, subject to their preservation and interpretation. Repetition of a unit can result from folding, faulting, an incorrect correlation, or combinations. An apparently symmetric two-dimensional outcrop may cut an asymmetric three-dimensional structure obliquely.

Cleavage/bedding relationships, lineations, thickness changes, unconformities, and cross-cutting fabrics can constrain the sequence of deformation. An axial-planar fabric is a hypothesis tied to an identified fold generation; several events can leave superficially similar orientations. Preserve observations that contradict a single-event explanation.

**Work:** complete both fold-analysis labs and their geometrical constructions. Use independent facing indicators to interpret a selected published section. Draw two admissible three-dimensional geometries for incomplete exposure, then identify which observation would distinguish them. Reconstruct a minimum event sequence for one overprinting example without assigning unsupported numerical ages.

Read the entire folds discussion with the primary-structure and fabrics sections. Later sections and restoration will require the same habit: make the observed relationships inspectable before judging whether a geometric model and its proposed mechanical history are mutually compatible.

**Continue:** [Infer fault displacement and sequence without equating separation with slip](Faults-fractures-and-slip-evidence.lingua#r_7GZYF6WKSDK43K38TBXHVNZ1YC).

